{% block article %}
    <article id="blog-post">
        <h1>Performance Optimizations</h1>
        <hr/>
        <p>
            From July 10 to 12, we organized the first Flow PHP hackathon together with
            <a href="https://github.com/stloyd" target="_blank">Józef (@stloyd)</a>
            and <a href="https://github.com/mrhdolek" target="_blank">Aleksander (@MrHDOLEK)</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
            We had one goal: improve general Flow performance. We created a dedicated GitHub label for the event that
            groups together all the work we pushed through those 3 days. Those changes also pushed me to redesign Flow's
            serialization/hydration architecture and invent a new binary data format, called Floe.
        </p>
        <p>
            GitHub Label: <a href="https://github.com/flow-php/flow/pulls?q=is%3Apr+label%3Ahackaton-07-2026+" target="_blank">hackaton-07-2026</a>
        </p>
        <h2>Benchmarks</h2>
